let me just ask you  again  when are you going to tell the prime  minister that he himself is the  principal object  that stands in the way of your doing  your job successfully which is to get  the conservative party re-elected to  government well i do not believe that  the prime minister should resign for the  the reasons that we have discussed in  this interview i do though think it is  essential that we address the kind of  failings that allow this to happen that  the prime minister is held to account  for what happened and addresses that in  parliament and that we also  build on the kind of work that we have  done with the vaccine rollout program to  address the subsequent challenges of  covert whether that's clearing the nhs  backlog or rebuilding the economy i  think that that is the right approach  rather than going through a period of  divisive uh leadership contests which  is not the sense that i get of what  british people want us to be focusing on  they want us to focus on the job at hand  of dealing with omicron and then the  consequences of covert  oligarchs thank you very much
 

